      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 Wiley-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim.",
        "AbstractText": "Chiral spirocarbocyclic skeletons are ubiquitous in natural products. An intramolecular Tsuji-Trost (T-T) α-allylation of simple cyclic ketones is a reasonable approach to construct chiral spriocarbocyclic motifs; however, it has been a challenging approach despite many excellent intermolecular examples. For the first time, this has been achieved by a Ru/H+ combined catalyst that dehydratively cyclizes racemic allylic alcohols comprising a simple ketone via simultaneous activation of the C=O and OH groups. This chiral technology facilitates the construction of various spirocarbocycles containing two contiguous spiro all-carbon quaternary and tertiary stereocenters. Among four possible stereoisomers, one stereoisomer can be selectively produced in high yield, enhancing the feasibility of the T-T strategy, particularly in the synthesis of spirocarbocycles."
      },
